meta {
  name: 02 Save Report Printing Settings
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/branch-settings/report-printing
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "isLabTestNotesSelectable": true,
    "isLabPanelNotesSelectable": false
  }
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("echoes back the saved pair", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    expect(d.isLabTestNotesSelectable).to.equal(true);
    expect(d.isLabPanelNotesSelectable).to.equal(false);
  });
}

docs {
  Save the active branch's report-printing settings. Both fields are optional: a
  switch that is left out keeps its current value (or `true` if the branch has never
  saved). The response is the resulting pair.

  - `isLabTestNotesSelectable` (boolean) - for a single lab test.
  - `isLabPanelNotesSelectable` (boolean) - for a test that belongs to a lab panel.

  Takes effect on the next screen load and the next print of any report held by this
  branch: the technician's checkboxes beside each Notes section appear or disappear
  (`GET /lab-reports/:id` -> `notesPrint.enabled`), and a switch that is OFF makes
  every Notes section print (see `PATCH /lab-reports/:id/note-print-sections`).

  Needs `branch_admin:branch_settings__update_branch_settings` (403 without it).
  Unknown fields, including `branchId`, are rejected with 400: the branch is always
  the caller's active branch from the JWT. Audited under
  `AuditModule.TECHNICIAN_SETTINGS`.

  These two switches are NOT part of `PUT /technician-settings` any more.
}
